# PUSH — Push Unaware Serving Host at {{.BaseURL}}

> A self-hosted Web Push scheduler for Progressive Web Apps that knows nothing. A PWA tells it "push this opaque ID to this device at this time"; at that time the server sends an end-to-end encrypted push `{"id": "<opaque id>", "t": <unix seconds>}` and the PWA's service worker looks the reminder text up locally (IndexedDB) and shows the notification. The server never sees reminder text, user names or accounts.

This file is written for AI coding agents (and their humans). It contains, in one read, everything needed to integrate a PWA with this server: instance facts, a step-by-step procedure, the full integration guide, the full HTTP API reference, and the source of the reusable browser client and of an example service worker.

